      any of this module's surfaces — orchestrator signature,
      per-step builder, helper — restores the retired in-code
      path-routing the schema collapse already retired."
    - >-
      "provisionBrain does not introspect `mcpServerConfig.args` to
      extract slot semantics. It reads `args` only as opaque bytes —
      passing them byte-for-byte through parseBrainAide and
      interpolateArgs into the MCP step's prescription, including any
      YAML null entries unchanged. It never reads `args[N]` for any
      named integer N to extract a brain root path, validate a path,
      check a token shape, sniff connector identity, or branch on
      slot meaning. Slot-semantic knowledge — which arg index is a
      path, which is a token, which is a URI — lives exclusively in
      the per-integration `config` body section, owned by the user.
      provisionBrain is backend-blind at the slot level."
    - >-
      "provisionBrain is invoked from exactly two callers under the
      rework, and consumes the two-step output the same way at each:
      (1) `aide_init({ category: \"brain\" })`, fired by
