      idempotency signal, byte drift is not. cli/init does NOT apply
      step 2 (sync owns `.mcp.json` brain writes downstream);
      `/aide:brain config` does not apply step 2 directly either —
      the integration prose wires the MCP entry by running sync after
      the user fills the null slot. The shape of the InitStep output
      is identical regardless of caller; consumer-shape detail of how
      each caller applies which subset of the two steps is the
      caller's concern, not provisionBrain's."
    - >-
      "Brain.aide is scaffolded with idempotent presence-only
      checking. When the file already exists at
      `.aide/config/brain.aide`, the step is exists regardless of
      byte drift from the bundled template — once the file lands,
      the user owns it forever and provisionBrain never proposes
