- `.aide/handoff.aide` -- Stage 3-prep architectural snapshot
  written 2026-04-28 mid-rework; decision #21 settles
  provisionBrain's two-step shape, decision #25 establishes
  per-integration ownership of arg-index slot semantics, and
  the "Where this cycle stopped" section captures the
  PATH_SLOT_INDEX / resolveBrainRoot rejection that drove the
  rework. Drove the Strategy beats on the two-step contract,
  the four-artifacts-move-to-prose rationale, and the
  no-`args[N]`-introspection invariant; drove the Bad-example
  triplet on `PATH_SLOT_INDEX`, `resolveBrainRoot`, and
  `argSlots`.
- `.aide/intent.aide` (root spec) -- Establishes the load-bearing
  invariants this module inherits: `mcpServerConfig.args` typed
  `(string | null)[]` with YAML null as the structural
  unwired-slot signal (no literal sentinel), the `.aide/config/`
  directory-wide ownership boundary, sync as the only mutation
  surface for `.mcp.json` (with null-refusal at the boundary),
  the unconditional `aide_init({ category: "brain" })` call
  from `/aide:brain config`, the four required entry-point
  artifacts seeded by integration prose, and the
  storage-agnostic vocabulary rule. Drove the YAML-null-not-
  sentinel Strategy paragraph (with the `aide-fresh` regression
  citation), the directory-wide ownership invariant, the
  presence-only idempotency rule, and the dual-caller apply
  pattern.
- `src/service/install/.aide` (immediate parent) -- Establishes
  that the install service is consumer-agnostic and shared by
  `aide_init` and cli/init, that the brain MCP entry's
  command/args are derived from the user-owned brain.aide via
  parseBrainAide rather than constructed inline, and that the
  package never owns launcher bytes. Drove the Strategy beat
  that brain.aide is the single source of truth for launcher
  bytes and the inline-launcher Bad-example rejection.
- `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide` -- Sibling spec: the parser
  whose typed frontmatter result preserves null entries verbatim
  in `mcpServerConfig.args`, plus the `interpolateArgs` helper
  that walks the args without coercing null. Drove the
  byte-faithful-forwarding Strategy paragraph and the
  defensive-null-replacement Bad-example.
- `src/service/install/provisionBrain/obsidianBrainAideTemplate/`
  (sibling helper) -- Owns the bundled default brain.aide
  template: collapsed two-field frontmatter, platform-branched
  launcher invocation, static YAML null at the unwired slot of
  `mcpServerConfig.args`, and the byte content of all six
  marker-bounded body sections. Takes no `brainPath` argument;
  the unwired slot is structurally null in every emission.
  Drove the cold-install Good example (frontmatter shape) and
  the no-`brainPath`-parameter Strategy beat.
- `src/cli/init/.aide` (sibling spec) -- Establishes cli/init's
  new role as cold-install caller of provisionBrain (apply
  step 1 only, never step 2; sync owns `.mcp.json` brain
  writes). Drove the dual-caller-architecture Strategy
  paragraph and the cli/init-applies-step-2 Bad-example.
- `src/cli/sync/.aide` (sibling spec) -- Establishes sync's
  null-refusal precondition at the `.mcp.json` boundary (sync
  exits non-zero if any `mcpServerConfig.args` element is null,
  no coercion). Drove the load-bearing safety-net half of the
  plans/agent-fills/sync-writes Strategy paragraph.
- `src/service/buildBrainState/.aide` (sibling spec) -- Establishes
  the four-state boot reporter vocabulary (`ok`, `no-brain-aide`,
  `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`) with null-args collapsing into
  `no-mcp-entry` BEFORE drift comparison. Drove the steady-state
  and MCP-drift Good examples (the status state vocabulary the
